abstract: "A Windows-native, freestanding C23 artificial-life simulation engine with 22 selectable core modules, 4 NASM AVX2/AVX-VNNI twins, a 41,817 B pure-integer CUDA PTX backend, 77/77 CTest targets, 164/164 GPU differential checks, and 38 Lean 4.35.0 declarations (26 substantive model, boundary, witness, and adversarial refutation theorems including the implemented core/az_chem.c a/4 decreasing-budget spread rule, plus 12 explicitly labeled definitional, constant, congruence, or legacy arithmetic sanity checks) checked locally by six Lean checkers and in Ubuntu CI by lean4lean and lake comparator under bubblewrap. The C23, NASM, and PTX code is not verified in Lean. Independent technical preprint (not peer-reviewed); 0 / 1,900 Mega-Atlas open problems retired."
